  "caption": "Quinn signed up for a charity walk, and by week two the big toe had opinions. Barefoot at home? Even worse.\n\nEvery step ends with the big toe bending up to push off. When that joint is stiff (often from gradual arthritis), push-off can get sore. Turf toe is different: a sprain from the toe being bent back hard.\n\nThings that often help: stiffer-soled shoes, calf and foot strengthening, building walking distance and hills gradually, and not forcing a stiff toe into painful stretches.\n\nIf the toe was bent back hard and won't take weight, or there's big swelling or a change in shape, get it checked. Pain that limits your day is worth assessing too.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
